  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CuSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi></math> is coordinated with 4 water molecules and two more oxygen atoms from Sulphate ion.</p><p>Now fifth water molecule is hydrogen-bonded and is deeply embedded in a crystal. It is not coordinated.</p><p>Only 4 water molecules are coordinated and the fifth is the only hydrogen bonded.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8d6a163e-4a00-4045-9e8e-b1eff983dacb-image.png\" style=\"width: 382px; height: 256px;\" /></p>",
